# Python scripts can be pinned by content hash (see `[python.scripts.*]` in a
# project manifest, sclpl/project/scripts.py). A hash pinned against LF content
# must not silently become CRLF on a Windows checkout, or every such script
# fails its own tamper check for no reason. Force LF for the files that are
# ever hashed this way.
*.py text eol=lf
